{
  "schema": "loom.scientific-case/1",
  "id": "superposition/lyman",
  "kind": "superposition",
  "name": "lyman",
  "title": "Lyman-alpha: an atom that rings",
  "line": "Half in 1s, half in 2p: the charge sloshes up and down 2.5 million billion times a second, the motion that radiates ultraviolet light at 121.5 nm.",
  "equation": "psi(t) = (psi_1s e^(-i E1 t) + psi_2pz e^(-i E2 t)) / sqrt(2);  rho = (psi_1s\u00b2 + psi_2pz\u00b2 + 2 psi_1s psi_2pz cos((E2 - E1) t)) / 2",
  "domain": {
    "shape": [
      80,
      80,
      80
    ],
    "units": "bohr (atomic units); energies in hartree",
    "boundary": "u(0) = u(200 bohr) = 0; display box holds all but 1e-4 of the probability"
  },
  "parameters": {
    "states": [
      "1s",
      "2p_z"
    ],
    "weights": [
      0.5,
      0.5
    ],
    "box_half_width_bohr": 17.78,
    "cell_bohr": 0.4445,
    "level": 0.010952795274020504,
    "omega_hartree": 0.3749999975160961,
    "period_au": 16.755160930127456,
    "period_fs": 0.40528796163306385,
    "frequency_hz": 2467381453844838.0,
    "wavelength_nm": 121.50227421594843,
    "dipole_exact": 0.7449355390278032,
    "dipole_numerical": 0.7449608176807122,
    "frames_per_period": 24
  },
  "method": "Radial equation by three-point finite differences on a uniform 0.01-bohr grid to 200 bohr, lowest eigenpairs of the tridiagonal matrix (LAPACK), Richardson with h = 0.02; 3D field = u(r)/r times a real spherical harmonic, linear interpolation in r, cell-centred 80^3 grid; surfaces by surface nets with three Newton projections.",
  "limits": [
    "Non-relativistic hydrogen with an infinitely heavy nucleus: no fine structure, spin, Lamb shift or reduced-mass correction (the real Lyman-alpha line is at 121.567 nm, not 121.502 nm).",
    "The surface is where |psi| (or the square root of the density) crosses a level enclosing 90 % of the probability on the grid; the cloud has no edge.",
    "Each case has its own box size, so orbitals are not drawn to a common scale; the page states the box width in bohr."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "tools/radial.py": "8ef724738b3a7e36aaff0bbaca2c5edc4997fc4b7f845ad7c14c8552b14b238a"
  },
  "external_dependencies": {
    "lib/stemkit/core.py": "b799990d80948989d6525fdd0c8f16c4eec884e659105fd6bd5750d4cf977600",
    "lib/stemkit/mesh.py": "fe4ebf154d7f8d7eed0c26ca13c3143678d60c8dbe74de4e7230e78fa1a6e326"
  },
